# ─── Script Keybindings (conflict-free) ──────────────────────────

# Subtitles menu (uosc) — c = Subtitles
c        script-binding uosc/subtitles

# YouTube auto-subtitles on-demand menu — Ctrl+c
Ctrl+c   script-binding ytdl_sub_menu/open
Ctrl+C   script-binding ytdl_sub_menu/open

# Audio tracks & dubs menu (uosc) — a = Audio
a        script-binding uosc/audio

# History (memo) — h = History
h    script-binding memo-history

# SponsorBlock voting — B = Block (Upvote), Ctrl+b = Downvote.
# (No Ctrl+B line: mpv canonicalizes it to the same key as Ctrl+Shift+b,
#  which the layout backups own — "Sub title backdrop".)
B        script-binding sponsorblock_upvote
Ctrl+b   script-binding sponsorblock_downvote

# Subtitle sync (autosubsync) — n = syNc
n    script-binding autosubsync-menu

# Subtitle background box toggle (Netflix / YouTube translucent box <-> transparent Cinema)
# OSD shows "Subtitle backdrop: on/off" via scripts/sub_backdrop.lua
b    script-binding sub_backdrop/toggle

# ─── Keyboard layout (Arabic 101 twins) ────────────────────────────
# mpv matches a binding against the CHARACTER a key produces ("mpv uses
# input translated by the current OS keyboard layout, rather than
# physical scan codes" - the manual), so letter bindings die under an
# Arabic layout. At deploy time mpv-config regenerates a twin block at
# the END of this file: for every printable binding, the character the
# SAME physical key produces on Arabic 101 (c -> ؤ, a -> ش, n -> ى,
# ? -> ؟, ...). Write only Latin lines here; the twins are automatic.
#
# The Ctrl+Shift+<letter> combos below are the only route to five
# actions under Arabic: h g b G B cannot have bare twins (measured on
# the real key stream: b and h deliver the IDENTICAL character - the
# lam-alef lam never reaches mpv). Under Arabic the combos arrive as
# Ctrl+<Arabic char> (Ctrl+Shift+H -> Ctrl+أ - measured), and the
# generator binds those twins too, so the SAME combos work in every
# layout:
Ctrl+Shift+h   script-binding memo-history
Ctrl+Shift+m   script-binding sponsorblock_set_segment
Ctrl+Shift+s   script-binding sponsorblock_submit_segment
Ctrl+Shift+b   script-binding sub_backdrop/toggle
Ctrl+Shift+u   script-binding sponsorblock_upvote

# Under Arabic, SHIFT+<letter> (no Ctrl!) delivers the shift-layer Arabic
# character - and those are distinct for our five keys. These lines give
# h m s b u a BARE-ish route (just hold Shift) in the Arabic layout; in
# the English layout the same presses produce plain uppercase letters, so
# nothing changes there. (Shift+G delivers the same أ as Shift+H - the
# mark action lives on Shift+M / Ctrl+Shift+M.)
أ   script-binding memo-history
’   script-binding sponsorblock_set_segment
ٍ   script-binding sponsorblock_submit_segment
آ   script-binding sub_backdrop/toggle
‘   script-binding sponsorblock_upvote

# Explicit Latin bindings for SponsorBlock segment marking
g        script-binding sponsorblock_set_segment
G        script-binding sponsorblock_submit_segment

# Instant play from clipboard — Ctrl+ر was retired: Windows control codes
# make it unreachable; Latin Ctrl+v / Ctrl+Shift+v cover it.
